'''Bosses''' are a unique enemy class outfitted with superior weapons, high health, rechargeable shields, special abilities, and other traits. They are far stronger than regular units as they will use varying strategies to deal damage and avoid taking it.

There are seven types of bosses in the game:
*[[#Normal Bosses|Normal Boss]] - Bosses which can be mostly found as the target of [[Assassination]] missions, AKA '''Grand Boss'''.
*[[#Field Bosses|Field Boss]] - Bosses that can be encountered on non-Assassination mission types, though not usually the main objective.
*[[#Hardmode Bosses|Hardmode Boss]] - Significantly harder bosses activated through additional steps.
*[[#Assassin Bosses|Assassin]] - Bosses that actively hunt down players who possess their respective [[Death Mark]]s.
*[[#Adversaries|Adversary]] - Randomized nemesis-style bosses with Warframe-like abilities that attempt to take control of the [[Star Chart]] or [[Höllvania]].
*[[#Quest Bosses|Quest Boss]] - Bosses that appear in [[Quests]] ('''not''' [[Events]]), are generally '''not''' farmable, and are '''not''' seen again in normal gameplay.
*[[#Event Bosses|Event Boss]] - Bosses that appear in [[Events]] ('''not''' [[Quests]]), are generally farmable, and are seen either once or periodically (depending on the event).

==Normal Bosses==
These Bosses are found mostly on [[Assassination]] missions (with a few exceptions), and are <u>unavoidable main objectives</u>. Each boss usually has a set of lines to "taunt" the Tenno sent to kill them. They generally drop [[mods]] and [[resources]] upon death. Depending on which boss the player is fighting, [[Blueprints]] of [[Warframe]] parts and special [[Weapon]] parts will often be rewarded upon mission completion.

